            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Rehnquist, the case John J. Fellers v. United States (No. 02-6320) was heard in oral argument."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner (Waxman)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ad9797ec722593b68c1ac8140c40d9cdec4bff17e406a7bb3a7151b6990aece9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ad9797ec7225-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner (Waxman), according to Petitioner (Waxman), the petitioner argues that the case concerns the Sixth Amendment right to counsel, not the Fifth Amendment Miranda right."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondent",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ad9797ec722593b68c1ac8140c40d9cdec4bff17e406a7bb3a7151b6990aece9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ad9797ec7225-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The respondent contends that the Eighth Circuit applied the wrong standard by focusing on interrogation rather than the Sixth Amendment test set in Rhode Island v. Innis."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Government",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ad9797ec722593b68c1ac8140c40d9cdec4bff17e406a7bb3a7151b6990aece9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ad9797ec7225-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The government says the \u201cdeliberate elicitation\u201d standard is confusing and differs from the interrogation standard used for Miranda."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ad9797ec722593b68c1ac8140c40d9cdec4bff17e406a7bb3a7151b6990aece9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ad9797ec7225-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 30,
              "start": 30
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "ad9797ec722593b68c1ac8140c40d9cdec4bff17e406a7bb3a7151b6990aece9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ad9797ec7225-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The court notes that after the petitioner was taken to jail, he received full Miranda warnings, voluntarily waived his right to counsel, and that any evidence derived from his statements must be suppressed unless the government shows sufficient attenuation."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner (Waxman)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ad9797ec722593b68c1ac8140c40d9cdec4bff17e406a7bb3a7151b6990aece9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ad9797ec7225-0000-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The court also states that the fruits of the statement must be suppressed under the Nix and Wade precedents."
      }
    ],
